WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:18.955
must have annoyed the other gods last night," Julia murmured to Markos.

2
00:00:20.055 --> 00:00:21.416
It was the following day.

3
00:00:22.476 --> 00:00:27.599
Julia and Markos were in the gymnasium, sitting on their usual bench watching Brody's training.

4
00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:30.880
Today Brody was practicing boxing.

5
00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.175
He'd spent the past few minutes sparring against Hermes himself.

6
00:00:36.716 --> 00:00:43.601
Markos gasped as Hermes landed yet another jab on Brody's shoulder, and Brody fell back with a grunt.

7
00:00:43.621 --> 00:00:47.044
"And now Brody is paying the price.

8
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:52.969
None of the other gods would agree to train with us today, so Hermes had no choice but

9
00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:54.730
to serve as Brody's opponent himself."

10
00:00:55.691 --> 00:01:00.135
Julia watched as Hermes danced around, jabbing at Brody every chance he got.

11
00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:01.576
She winced.

12
00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:05.686
The messenger god seemed to be enjoying himself.

13
00:01:06.686 --> 00:01:12.710
He flitted back and forth, taking advantage of his greater height, speed, and strength, as well as his

14
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:13.731
winged sandals.

15
00:01:14.691 --> 00:01:20.215
So far Brody hadn't landed a single punch, although he'd received plenty from Hermes.

16
00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:23.176
"Ugh," Julia said.

17
00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:24.878
"I hate boxing.

18
00:01:25.178 --> 00:01:26.058
It's so violent!"

19
00:01:26.078 --> 00:01:28.500
"Good one, Brody!"

20
00:01:29.052 --> 00:01:34.334
Markos shouted as Brody swung at Hermes' chin, barely missing as the god spun out of the way.

21
00:01:34.354 --> 00:01:38.516
"Er, I mean, nicely dodged, Hermes."

22
00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:40.577
Hermes grinned.

23
00:01:40.597 --> 00:01:45.899
"Don't hesitate to cheer for your mortal friend, boy," he called to Markos good-naturedly.

24
00:01:45.919 --> 00:01:48.580
"He needs all the help he can get!"

25
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.442
"Urgh!" Brody grunted, lunging at Hermes.

26
00:01:54.863 --> 00:01:57.204
But once again his punch missed the mark.

27
00:01:58.224 --> 00:02:02.346
Hermes sidestepped easily and hit Brody on the ear as Brody went by.

28
00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:07.048
"I don't want to watch anymore," Julia told Markos with a shudder.

29
00:02:07.988 --> 00:02:12.550
She glanced around for something else to do, but the gymnasium was nearly deserted.

30
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:16.691
"Let's go to the agora and find out if Alcides has arrived yet.

31
00:02:17.732 --> 00:02:19.713
Today is the day he's supposed to arrive, right?"

32
00:02:20.993 --> 00:02:24.034
Markos was leaning forward, watching the fight with interest.

33
00:02:24.054 --> 00:02:27.776
"Alcides is not in Olympia yet," he said.

34
00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:30.665
"If he were here, we'd have heard about it."

35
00:02:31.745 --> 00:02:33.505
Julia sighed and sat back.

36
00:02:36.006 --> 00:02:41.668
She looked away as Hermes punched Brody in the nose, sending sweat and a little blood flying.

37
00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.209
Now she could see that Apollo was wandering toward them.

38
00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:51.110
"Nice moves, Hermes," Apollo said.

39
00:02:51.131 --> 00:02:56.012
"It's a good thing you're getting your champion used to losing.

40
00:02:57.216 --> 00:03:00.237
He'll be doing a lot of it once the Games start!"

41
00:03:01.377 --> 00:03:03.098
Hermes frowned at the other god.

42
00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:09.199
But before he could say a word, the ground beneath the gymnasium let out an ominous rumble.

43
00:03:09.219 --> 00:03:11.260
"What was that?"

44
00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.940
Julia exclaimed.

45
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.121
"An earthquake?"

46
00:03:15.581 --> 00:03:17.822
Suddenly the ground split open.

47
00:03:18.342 --> 00:03:20.222
Dirt and sand sprayed everywhere.

48
00:03:21.063 --> 00:03:25.824
Hermes and Apollo jumped back as a chasm appeared in the spot where they'd been standing.

49
00:03:26.828 --> 00:03:31.452
Brody just stood there staring, and Hermes had to fly in and grab him so he didn't fall

50
00:03:31.492 --> 00:03:32.253
into the chasm.

51
00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:35.255
"What's going on?"

52
00:03:35.736 --> 00:03:37.958
Julia cried, grabbing Markos by the arm.

53
00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.980
Markos' face had gone pale.

54
00:03:41.581 --> 00:03:42.161
He pointed.

55
00:03:42.181 --> 00:03:43.823
"Hades is here."

56
00:03:45.064 --> 00:03:49.207
The chasm belched out black smoke, and then a god stepped out.

57
00:03:49.227 --> 00:03:54.632
"Hades," Julia whispered, impressed and a little scared.

58
00:03:55.372 --> 00:03:57.154
"The god of the underworld!"

59
00:03:58.274 --> 00:04:05.640
Hades' chest and shoulders were broad, and he had pale skin, sleek dark hair, and a craggy, ugly

60
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.544
face. He was holding a chain in one strong hand.

61
00:04:11.125 --> 00:04:15.829
The other end of the chain was fastened to the collar of the largest dog Julia had ever

62
00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:19.291
seen. But this was no ordinary dog.

63
00:04:19.832 --> 00:04:22.974
It had three heads and a serpent for a tail.

64
00:04:22.994 --> 00:04:26.813
"Is that is that Cerberus?"

65
00:04:27.474 --> 00:04:29.836
Julia asked Markos in a shaky voice.

66
00:04:29.856 --> 00:04:34.119
"The three-headed dog that guards the gates of the underworld?"

67
00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:35.981
"Of course!"

68
00:04:36.521 --> 00:04:37.222
Markos said.

69
00:04:38.723 --> 00:04:43.147
Brody hurried over to his friends, staying far away from the edge of the chasm.

70
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.348
"What's going on?"

71
00:04:45.809 --> 00:04:46.349
he asked.

72
00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.972
He spit out a mouthful of saliva mixed with blood.

73
00:04:51.173 --> 00:04:52.274
"Who is that?"

74
00:04:52.294 --> 00:04:56.257
"Hades," Julia told him with a shiver.

75
00:04:56.277 --> 00:04:58.658
"He's the god of the underworld."

76
00:04:58.678 --> 00:05:01.079
"The underworld?"

77
00:05:01.479 --> 00:05:02.260
Brody echoed.

78
00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.221
Markos nodded.

79
00:05:04.241 --> 00:05:07.262
"It's where the dead go after their lives are over.

80
00:05:07.923 --> 00:05:08.983
It's known as Hades."

81
00:05:10.124 --> 00:05:13.365
Brody shook his head and looked at Markos in confusion.

82
00:05:13.385 --> 00:05:18.528
"Okay, Hermes hit me pretty hard a few times," he said.

83
00:05:19.688 --> 00:05:25.830
"But did you really just say that guy's name is Hades—and the place he comes from is also

84
00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:26.750
called Hades?"

85
00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:34.352
"That's right," Julia said, wondering if Brody had paid any attention at all in social studies class.

86
00:05:35.413 --> 00:05:36.853
Brody snorted with laughter.

87
00:05:36.873 --> 00:05:40.014
"Hades from Hades!

88
00:05:40.394 --> 00:05:40.994
Good one!"

89
00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:47.276
Julia rolled her eyes and turned to watch as Hades looped Cerberus' chain around a column.

90
00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:54.502
"Guard this entrance," Hades commanded the three-headed dog, pointing to the chasm.

91
00:05:54.522 --> 00:05:58.083
"Do not let the dead escape!"

92
00:05:59.483 --> 00:06:00.944
Julia's eyes widened.

93
00:06:00.964 --> 00:06:04.485
"Can the dead really escape from the underworld?"

94
00:06:04.925 --> 00:06:06.185
she whispered to Markos.

95
00:06:06.205 --> 00:06:08.146
"They can try.

96
00:06:08.586 --> 00:06:14.728
That's why Hades usually visits the surface through the entrance that lies across the river Acheron," Markos whispered

97
00:06:14.768 --> 00:06:19.910
back. "He must be in a hurry if he decided to open a portal here in Olympia."

98
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.452
Hermes and Apollo looked perfectly relaxed as Hades stepped toward them.

99
00:06:25.472 --> 00:06:29.294
"Greetings, Hades," Apollo said.

100
00:06:29.314 --> 00:06:32.935
"What brings you to this side of the Earth's surface?"

101
00:06:34.676 --> 00:06:35.817
Hades greeted them.

102
00:06:35.837 --> 00:06:37.777
"It is good to see you.

103
00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:43.060
I am here to see the champion my brother Zeus claims is the best he's ever seen.

104
00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.683
I hear this amazing mortal has just arrived in Olympia."

105
00:06:50.344 --> 00:06:52.205
"What?" Hermes exclaimed.

106
00:06:52.225 --> 00:06:53.966
"Why didn't we know of this?"

107
00:06:55.107 --> 00:06:55.987
Apollo smirked.

108
00:06:57.188 --> 00:07:02.211
"Ah, so the messenger of the gods is the last to receive this particular message, huh?

109
00:07:02.711 --> 00:07:03.952
Too bad, Hermes."

110
00:07:05.653 --> 00:07:07.134
Hades laughed loudly.

111
00:07:14.148 --> 00:07:16.410
"Never mind," Hades went on.

112
00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:22.355
"If Zeus isn't here, perhaps he is bringing his hero to the agora first."

113
00:07:23.716 --> 00:07:27.919
Hermes' scowl disappeared, replaced by an eager expression.

114
00:07:27.939 --> 00:07:30.621
"What are we waiting for?"

115
00:07:31.081 --> 00:07:31.602
he cried.

116
00:07:31.622 --> 00:07:34.124
"Let's go to the agora at once!"
